SciPy 1.18.1 on WebAssembly with OpenBLAS's C translation of LAPACK: two
declarations wasm-ld links to traps, proposed upstream, not filed.

- _common_array_utils.hh declares ?getrf and ?getri returning CBLAS_INT;
  they are LAPACK subroutines, which SciPy's other declarations (cython_lapack,
  _common_array_utils.h) and LAPACK declare void, and nothing reads the
  value. WebAssembly checks a call's type: scipy.linalg.inv and det trapped.
- trlib passes dlagtm a hidden string length after LDB, gfortran's
  convention; no other SciPy call passes one, and a LAPACK built from C
  (OpenBLAS's C_LAPACK) takes none.

